And the exact frequency you get depends on the Doppler shift on that place. Doppler shift meaning like a-- like a train whistle, where it-- if there are still train whistles-- you come in, you get a high pitch. You go away, the thing goes past. So say it's a-- it's a truck. You have a truck with a-- beeping its horn or something. It's higher pitched as it comes towards you and then lower pitched when it goes away.

So the pitch of something is changed by velocity. And so that-- so the pitch or the wavelength is changed by the velocity of objects. You measure the velocity the object from other ways, you can measure the distances, you can measure something about the-- you can measure something about the absolute brightness, perhaps you're absolutely referring how far away it is, if it's in our galaxy, outside the galaxy.

